        <div class="mh-eyebrow">The Origin</div>
        <h2 class="mh-about-origin-headline">Born from 25+ Years of Global Enterprise Experience</h2>
        <p>Most platforms start with a feature idea. MedhaIQ started with a pattern noticed over twenty-five years leading global consulting practices, enterprise transformations, and talent initiatives across North America, EMEA, and APAC.</p>
        <p>Technical skill opens the door — but the ability to structure an argument, read a room, and communicate under pressure decides how far someone walks through it. The professionals who made the strongest impression were rarely the ones who knew the most; they were the ones who stayed clear and composed when the questions got hard.</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="mh-about-gaps">
        <li class="mh-about-gap">
          <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">01</span>
          <div>
            <div class="mh-about-gap-title">Feedback arrives too late.</div>
            <p class="mh-about-gap-text">A rejection email or annual review tells you what happened after the opportunity has already passed.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="mh-about-gap">
          <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">02</span>
          <div>
            <div class="mh-about-gap-title">The first real attempt happens at the highest stakes.</div>
            <p class="mh-about-gap-text">Professionals are expected to perform in interviews, presentations and leadership moments without having practiced under realistic pressure.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="mh-about-gap">
          <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">03</span>
          <div>
            <div class="mh-about-gap-title">Evaluation is often subjective.</div>
            <p class="mh-about-gap-text">Careers can turn on impressions such as "not senior enough" or "good communicator" without giving people evidence they can understand and improve.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mh-about-origin-close">MedhaIQ exists to close that gap. By pairing enterprise-grade evaluation standards with adaptive AI, we built the environment we wished existed twenty-five years ago: a place to practice honestly, get evaluated rigorously, and walk into the real moment already having done the hard part once before.</p>

